gnostics on\n   the error paths are only safe because those paths exit non-zero; do not add\n   chatter to the success path.\n4. Stay within the existing single `package main` / `func main` CLI shape in\n   this file. No new packages, no new files, no dependency additions — the\n   service is reached only as a process by `go run ./services/calc`, so the\n   module layout must keep that entry point working from the repository root.\n\n**Negative sign to respect:** do not \"fix\" this by making the argument default\nor by special-casing the value `3`. The behaviour must be the general doubling\nrule, so the CLI is correct for any integer the documented schema admits\n(including `0` and negatives, which `strconv.Atoi` accepts and the CLI document\ndoes not exclude).\n\n## Tests each part serves\n\n- Part 1 is the whole repair and serves the single test in this set,\n  `/go-test/go-test:fixture.stepsrun.tests.calc::TestCalc001Double`\n  (`tests/calc/calc_test.go`, scenario `calc-001-double`). Its step 3,\n  `Then the result is 6`, currently fails with `expected 6, got 3`; after the\n  change the `double` subprocess returns `6` for input `3`, step 3 passes, and\n  `s.Done()` still validates the stated steps against the registry — which is\n  untouched, so that check keeps passing.\n\n## Out of scope / do not touch\n\n- `tests/calc/calc_test.go`, `tests/calc/steps/register.go`,\n  `tests/calc/steps/state.go`, `tests/calc/scenarios/scenarios.go` — generated\n  test and step-definition code; no edits, and no weakening of the `result`\n  comparison or of `Done()`'s registry check.\n- `docs/scenarios.yaml`, `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`,\n  `docs/architecture/calc-cli.yaml`, `docs/product/product.yaml` — specification\n  documents; the implementation must be bent to them, not the reverse. The\n  documents already describe the correct doubling behaviour, so no document\n  change is warranted.\n- `services/neighbour` — declared in the architecture but unused by this\n  